style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>HOIST ROPE SPEED TESTS:<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>Tests were conducted to verify the speed of
the hoist rope under various conditions.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>The hoist rope was marked (painted) in three 50-foot increments for a
total of 150 feet.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>The distance for each
increment and total distance traveled were timed with a stopwatch to the
nearest half second.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>Three tests were
conducted with the hoist operating at various speeds including the following:<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='tab-stops:13.5pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Test 1 � The speed at which
personnel usually travel through the open doors.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Test 2 � The speed at which
personnel travel when they are within 100 feet of any stop.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Test 3 � The maimum speed at
which personnel are lowered.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='tab-stops:13.5pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>During each of the tests the speed
indicated at the hoist operator's station was recorded along with a timed test
of the rope.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>Each test was conducted
twice and the results are shown in Table 2.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

