<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Additionally, the maimum
overspeed for lowering personnel in the shaft was verified.<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>Three tests were conducted by lowering the
bucket into the shaft at the maimum speed for personnel.<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>A tachometer was used to measure the rope
speed at the top of the shaft as the bucket was lowered.<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>The tachometer measurements of the rope speed
at the top of the shaft ranged from 450 to 465 fpm when the overspeed
controller activated.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>The speed
indicator inside the hoist house for each of the tests was approimately 500
fpm.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;tet-indent:-18.0pt;mso-pagination:
none;mso-list:l11 level1 lfo11;tab-stops:13.5pt list 36.0pt'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana;mso-fareast-font-family:Verdana;
mso-bidi-font-family:Verdana'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>5)<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>EQUIPMENT AND CONSTRUCTION
MATERIALS:<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>The sinking bucket was
typically used for lowering materials in the shaft.<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>Items that could not be readily lifted or
easily put into the bucket were rigged beneath it.<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>At the time of the accident, a 20-foot-long,
2-inch-wide nylon sling (SN 4230767) manufactured by Black Diamond Lifting
Products, Booneville, IN, was attached to the bottom of the bucket with a
shackle.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>The sling was rated for 11,000
pounds in a vertical hold, and 8,800 pounds in a choker hold position.<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>A similar shackle, model S-209, manufactured
by The Crosby Group Incorporated, was attached through the eye of the sling and
allowed to hang freely from the bottom of the bucket when the sling was not
being used.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>This shackle had an overall
length of 6.56 inches and a nominal diameter of 1 inch.<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'> </span><o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='tab-stops:13.5pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;tet-indent:-18.0pt;mso-pagination:
none;mso-list:l11 level1 lfo11;tab-stops:13.5pt list 36.0pt'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana;mso-fareast-font-family:Verdana;
mso-bidi-font-family:Verdana'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>6)<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>SHACKLE POSITION IN COLLAR
DOORS:<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>Based upon eyewitness accounts,
the shackle attached to the end of the 20-foot nylon sling (free end) was found
in one of the collar door horizontal beams immediately after the accident.<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>Given the geometry of the shaft opening and
assuming the bucket is oriented in the center of this opening when entering the
shaft, a range of horizontal distances and swing angles necessary for the
shackle to become caught in the collar door structure was determined.<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>The shackle would have to travel between 20 </span><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial'>&#8541;</span><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'> and 68 � �inches with swing angles
between 4.9 and 16.5 degrees (from vertical) to come to rest in the collar door
structure.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>MSHA investigators used the
interview information and eamined several positions of the shackle in the door
in an attempt to recreate a possible final position of the shackle.<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>Three positions of the shackle were eamined
in the collar doors.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>They are shown in Ehibits
4-6.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>For each of the shackle positions
eamined, a force was applied to the sling in the up and down direction to
simulate the travel direction of the bucket.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>
</span>Forces applied in the up and down direction to the sling as shown in
Position 1 (Ehibit 4) caused it to pull out of the beam.<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>Forces applied in the down direction to the
sling shown in Position 2 (Ehibit 5) caused it to pull out of the beam, while
forces applied in the up direction caused the shackle to wedge itself into the
beam, causing the sling to tighten.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>Forces applied in the up direction to the sling shown in Position 3
(Ehibit 6) caused it to pull out of the beam, while forces applied in the down
direction caused the shackle to wedge itself into the beam, causing the sling
to tighten.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>Based on these tests, it is consensus
of the accident investigation team that the sling was in Position 3, causing
the bucket to tip or overturn as it was lowered.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:18.0pt;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt;tet-indent:-18.0pt;mso-pagination:
none;mso-list:l11 level1 lfo11;tab-stops:13.5pt list 36.0pt'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana;mso-fareast-font-family:Verdana;
mso-bidi-font-family:Verdana'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>7)<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><![endif]><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>WEATHER AT THE TIME OF THE
ACCIDENT:<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>According to the <st1:place
w:st="on"><st1:City w:st="on">Mt. Carmel</st1:City>, <st1:State w:st="on">Illinois</st1:State></st1:place>
National Weather Station, the temperature at the time of the accident was
approimately 84 degrees and the wind was generally NNW between 6 and 10 MPH.<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span><o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><u><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>SHAFT SINKING PLAN</span></u><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>: <o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Frontier-Kemper's Shaft Sinking
Plan, which was in effect at the time of the accident, was approved on <st1:date
Year="2006" Day="12" Month="9" ls="trans" w:st="on">September 12, 2006</st1:date>.<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>The content for approval of Slope and Shaft
Sinking Plans is regulated by 30 CFR Section 77.1900(a).<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>The plan did not specifically address the use
of personal protective equipment to be utilized (fall protection) while in the
bucket, nor contain details of equipment and procedures to be utilized for
transporting supplies and materials (slings).<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>However, the use of fall
protection (belts) and the requirements for the transporting of supplies and
materials are mandated by 30 CFR Sections 77.1908(o) and 77.1908 (i),
respectively.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>The approved shaft sinking plan,
issued to Frontier-Kemper rather than the mine operator, was reviewed by the
accident investigation team.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>Based upon
the circumstances and preliminary findings of the accident investigation, it
was determined that Frontier- Kemper's plan should be revised to adequately
address the use of fall protection equipment and the transporting of supplies
and materials.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>In order to address the
investigators'  concerns and to prevent a similar occurrence, the District 8 Manager
requested the plan be revised.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Additional safety precautions were
added to the shaft sinking plan to further enhance the safety of the miners
throughout the shaft sinking operation and included the following:<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:108.0pt;tet-indent:-18.0pt;mso-pagination:
none;mso-list:l3 level1 lfo14;tab-stops:13.5pt list 108.0pt'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;
mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>�<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]><span style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>All
persons shall use a suitable full harness and be tied off when riding in the
shaft sinking bucket.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:108.0pt;tet-indent:-18.0pt;mso-pagination:
none;mso-list:l3 level1 lfo14;tab-stops:13.5pt list 108.0pt'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;
mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>�<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]><span style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>When
entering and eiting the shaft sinking bucket at the work deck, all persons
shall be tied off.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>All persons must
remain tied off to the bucket until they are tied off to the deck.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:108.0pt;tet-indent:-18.0pt;mso-pagination:
none;mso-list:l3 level1 lfo14;tab-stops:13.5pt list 108.0pt'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;
mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>�<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]><span style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Adequate
fall protection shall be in place or used when personnel are working on the
work deck, such as a third cable rail.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:108.0pt;tet-indent:-18.0pt;mso-pagination:
none;mso-list:l3 level1 lfo14;tab-stops:13.5pt list 108.0pt'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;
mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>�<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]><span style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>A
means shall be provided for safe footing when persons are embarking or
disembarking from the sinking bucket at the work deck, such as a chain securing
the bucket to the deck.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:108.0pt;tet-indent:-18.0pt;mso-pagination:
none;mso-list:l3 level1 lfo14;tab-stops:13.5pt list 108.0pt'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;
mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>�<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]><span style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Permissible
wireless emergency communication devices shall be required between persons
riding the bucket, the hoistman and the toplander.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:108.0pt;tet-indent:-18.0pt;mso-pagination:
none;mso-list:l3 level1 lfo14;tab-stops:13.5pt list 108.0pt'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;
mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>�<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]><span style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Straps,
lanyards or rigging shall not be attached to the bottom of the bucket when
transporting persons.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:108.0pt;tet-indent:-18.0pt;mso-pagination:
none;mso-list:l3 level1 lfo14;tab-stops:13.5pt list 108.0pt'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;
mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>�<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]><span style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>When
transporting personnel in the shaft, the toplander or other personnel will be
stationed at the collar, in communication with the hoistman and be able to
visually observe the bucket until it descends past the collar doors.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:108.0pt;tet-indent:-18.0pt;mso-pagination:
none;mso-list:l3 level1 lfo14;tab-stops:13.5pt list 108.0pt'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;
mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>�<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]><span style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>The
speed of the buckets transporting persons shall not eceed 500 feet per minute
and not more than 200 feet per minute when within 100 feet of any stop per
Title 30 Code of Federal regulations, Part 77, Subpart T, Section 1908,
Paragraph (j).<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:108.0pt;tet-indent:-18.0pt;mso-pagination:
none;mso-list:l3 level1 lfo14;tab-stops:13.5pt list 108.0pt'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;
mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>�<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]><span style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>The
means for preventing these speeds shall be provided automatically by Lilly
controls or other similar means.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:108.0pt;tet-indent:-18.0pt;mso-pagination:
none;mso-list:l3 level1 lfo14;tab-stops:13.5pt list 108.0pt'><![if !supportLists]><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;
mso-bidi-font-family:Symbol'><span style='mso-list:Ignore'>�<span
style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><![endif]><span style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Training
shall be provided regarding these items and 5000-23 forms shall be completed
for the training.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:90.0pt;mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:
13.5pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<span style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";
mso-bidi-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:
EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA'><br clear=all style='page-break-before:always'>
</span>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>These  provisions were approved and made a part of the shaft
sinking plan on <st1:date Year="2007" Day="23" Month="8" ls="trans" w:st="on">August
 23, 2007</st1:date>.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span><o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><u><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>FALL PROTECTION-ANSI STANDARDS<o:p></o:p></span></u></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>As previously stated, at the time
of the accident Frontier-Kemper's approved plan did not address the use of full
body harness fall protection.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>Full body
harness protection is widely practiced throughout industry where fall hazards
of greater than four (4) feet are known to eist.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>At the time of the accident,
standards of the American National Standards Institute (ANSI) and MSHA's own
regulations, (30 C.F.R. Section 77.1710(g) and 77.1908(o)), did not
specifically address the use of <u>full body harness</u> fall protection in
these situations.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span><o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>In October 2007, ANSI implemented
new standards that now provide guidelines for fall prevention.<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>The ANSI Z359-2007 standard, which was not in
effect at the time of this accident, is designed to provide a proactive,
multi-faceted fall protection program with emphasis on training of both
supervisors and employees in work-at-heights activities.<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>Design of the work site with fall prevention
in mind is recommended as well as personal fall arrest systems when the
work-at-heights distance eceeds four feet.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>The accident investigation team
recommends that these standards be considered when formulating and evaluating
all future shaft and slope sinking plans.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><u><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>MECHANISM OF THE ACCIDENT:<o:p></o:p></span></u></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><u><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p><span style='tet-decoration:
 none'> <br></span></o:p></span></u></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>The use of the sling suspended
from the bottom edge of the bucket created a medium for the introduction of
eternal forces and, combined with the absence/non-use of properly attached
fall protection (belts), contributed to the fatal accident.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>A number of safety belts, with
attached lanyards, piled near the shaft collar and among the detritus of used
medical supplies and rescue equipment, were found by the investigation
team,.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>However, at that time it could
not be positively determined to whom the belts were assigned or belonged, or if
they had been in use by the victims at the time of the accident.<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>Interviews revealed that full body harness
fall protection, although available at the site, was not routinely used by
miners being transported in the bucket prior to the accident.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>A review of MSHA training videos
available at the time of the accident showed persons being transported in
sinking buckets, with and without use of fall protection.<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>However, the training videos did not show the
use of slings attached to the bucket while persons were being transported in
the bucket. <span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>These training materials
were recalled by MSHA following this accident.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>MSHA standards clearly address the
use of 'safety belts'  when persons are required to work in or over a shaft
where there is a drop of 10 or more feet.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>Use of safety belts in this instance may have either prevented or
mitigated the severity of this accident.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Use of the described sling, in and
of itself, is not directly contrary to any standard.<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>However, the presence of the unsecured sling
allowed for the loss of control of the bucket required by the standard found at
30 C.F.R. 1908-1.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>During interviews, it
was revealed that, prior to the accident, the sling and accompanying materials
and supplies, had been frequently attached to the sinking bucket while persons
were being transported in the bucket.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span><o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Due to the geometry and weight of
the sinking bucket, absent the eertion of eternal forces (sling), it is
highly improbable that the bucket could have sufficiently tipped or inverted, to
cause its contents to fall.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><u><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>TRAINING OF THE VICTIMS</span></u><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>:<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span><o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Frontier-Kemper's training records
were eamined by representatives of MSHA's Educational Field Services. The record
of eperienced miner training and task training for Ashmore and the hazard
training record for <st1:City w:st="on"><st1:place w:st="on">Richardson</st1:place></st1:City>
could not be produced. Due to the knowledge and eperience of the victims,
these deficiencies were deemed as non-contributory to the accident and were
cited separately.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='mso-pagination:none;tab-stops:13.5pt'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><span style='mso-tab-count:1'> </span><o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyTetIndent2 style='margin-top:24.0pt;margin-right:0pt;
margin-bottom:12.0pt;margin-left:0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>ROOT<a
name=RootCause></a> CAUSE ANALYSIS<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyTet style='margin-bottom:12.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'>An analysis was conducted to identify the most basic causes
of the accident that were correctable through reasonable management
controls.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>During the analysis, root
causes were identified that, if eliminated, would have either prevented the accident
or mitigated its consequences.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>The
following root causes were identified as a result of the investigation.<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>In each case, an effective management system,
procedure or policy was not in place to assure compliance with the regulation
or safe mining procedure.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyTet style='margin-bottom:12.0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together;
page-break-after:avoid'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Listed
below are root causes identified during the analysis and the respective
corrective actions implemented to prevent a recurrence of the accident:<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<ol style='margin-top:0pt' start=1 type=1>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-list:l10 level1 lfo6;tab-stops:list 36.0pt'><i
     style='mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
     font-family:Verdana'>Root Cause:</span></i><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
     font-family:Verdana'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>A nylon sling
     and shackle used for lowering supplies were left attached to the sinking
     bucket while transporting persons. <span
     style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>The lack of an effective administrative
     control to assure that etraneous objects were not attached to the bucket
     when transporting persons contributed to the loss of control of the hoist.<o:p></o:p></span></li>
</ol>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:18.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'><i style='mso-bidi-font-style:
normal'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Corrective Action:</span></i><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>The independent contractor's approved shaft sinking plan has been
revised to include provisions that persons will not be transported with
anything attached to the bucket.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<ol style='margin-top:0pt' start=2 type=1>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-list:l10 level1 lfo6;tab-stops:list 36.0pt'><i
     style='mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
     font-family:Verdana'>Root Cause:</span></i><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
     font-family:Verdana'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>The toplander
     was not at his duty station observing the mantrip as it passed through the
     collar doors.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>Inadequate policies
     and procedures resulted in the hoist operating without the toplander and
     contributed to the loss of control of the hoist.<o:p></o:p></span></li>
</ol>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:18.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'><i style='mso-bidi-font-style:
normal'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Corrective Action:</span></i><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>The independent contractor's approved shaft sinking plan has been
revised to require the toplander or other personnel to be stationed at the
collar, in communication with the hoistman and be able to visually observe the
bucket until it descends past the collar doors.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span><o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<ol style='margin-top:0pt' start=3 type=1>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='mso-list:l10 level1 lfo6;tab-stops:list 36.0pt'><i
     style='mso-bidi-font-style:normal'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
     font-family:Verdana'>Root Cause:</span></i><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
     font-family:Verdana'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>The independent
     contractor had no policy in place requiring the use of fall protection
     when personnel are transported in the sinking bucket.<o:p></o:p></span></li>
</ol>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:18.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span><o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'><i style='mso-bidi-font-style:
normal'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'>Corrective Action:</span></i><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>The independent contractor's approved shaft sinking plan has been
revised to include the use of fall protection when persons are transported in
the sinking bucket.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:36.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<h6 style='margin-top:24.0pt;margin-right:0pt;margin-bottom:12.0pt;margin-left:
0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan lines-together'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'>CONCLUSION<o:p></o:p></span></h6>

<p class=MsoBodyTetIndent2 align=left style='margin-left:0pt;tet-align:left'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana;font-weight:normal'>The accident
occurred as a result of Frontier-Kemper's</span><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'> </span><span style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana;
font-weight:normal'>failure to ensure that the hoist was under the control of
the hoistman at all times when persons were in the shaft.<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>The toplander was not at his station as the
bucket was being lowered through the shaft collar doors and the hoistman had no
visual contact with the bucket at this point.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>The hoistman lost control of the bucket when the nylon sling and shackle
entangled with the shaft collar door.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>The contractor also failed to ensure that adequate fall protection was
utilized while persons were transported in the sinking bucket.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyTetIndent2 align=left style='margin-left:0pt;tet-align:left'><span
style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana;font-weight:normal'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span><o:p></o:p></span></p>

<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:Verdana;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;
mso-bidi-language:AR-SA'><br clear=all style='page-break-before:always'>
</span></b>

<h1 style='margin-bottom:12.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:
Verdana'>ENFORCEMENT ACTIONS<o:p></o:p></span></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:18.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'>1. <span style='mso-tab-count:1'> </span>A 103(k) Order, <u>No.
7489388</u> was issued to ensure the safety of the miners until the
investigation could be completed. <br>
<br>
2.<span style='mso-tab-count:1'> </span>A 104(a) Citation, <u>No. 7502227</u>,
was issued to Frontier-Kemper Constructors Inc. for a violation of 30 CFR 77.
1908 � 1, stating that the independent contractor failed to ensure that the
hoist was under the control of the hoistman when men were in the shaft.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:18.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:18.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'>During the course of the investigation of a multiple
fatality accident which occurred on <st1:date Year="2007" Day="10" Month="8"
ls="trans" w:st="on">August 10, 2007</st1:date>, the following was revealed;<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:18.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:18.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'>The independent contractor failed to assure that the hoist
was under the control of a hoistman at all times when men were in the
shaft.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>The sinking bucket from which
three victims fell to their deaths was not visible to the hoistman, due to
distances and structural obstructions between the hoistman's operating station
and the shaft collar. In addition, the �toplander�, whose duties include
advising the hoistman of the positions of men and equipment, was not at his
station at the time of the accident.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>Finally, control of the hoist was lost when a sling and shackle,
attached to the bottom of the sinking bucket, became entangled with the shaft
collar door, resulting in the sinking bucket tipping over and causing three
victims to fall to their deaths.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>In
addition to the three persons in the sinking bucket, five other men were
working at or near the shaft bottom at the time of the accident and were
eposed.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:18.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'>3. A 104(a) Citation, <u>No. 7502228</u>, was issued to
Frontier-Kemper Constructors Inc. for a violation of 30 CFR 77.1908(o) stating
that the Contractor allowed persons to ride the sinking bucket without proper
fall protection.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:18.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'><span style='mso-tab-count:1'> </span><o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:18.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'>During the course of the investigation of a multiple
fatality accident which occurred on <st1:date ls="trans" Month="8" Day="10"
Year="2007" w:st="on">August 10, 2007</st1:date>, the following was revealed;<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:18.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:18.0pt'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:Verdana'>The independent contractor failed to require the use of
properly attached fall protection when persons were riding the sinking
bucket.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>Three persons traveling in the
sinking bucket fell approimately 550 feet to their deaths after the bucket
inverted.<span style='mso-spacerun:yes'>..... </span>None of the victims wore
properly attached fall protection.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><span style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:Verdana'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'><span style='font-size:11.0pt;
font-family:Verdana;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman";mso-bidi-font-family:
"Times New Roman";mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;
mso-bidi-language:AR-SA'><br clear=all style='page-break-before:always'>
</span></b>
